      "revision": 1368742850,
      "text": "Chrysalidocarpus basilongus is a species of flowering plant in the family Arecaceae. It is a palm tree endemic to Mount Vatovavy and nearby mountains in southeastern Madagascar. It grows in humid, mossy montane shrubland on flat-topped mountains and rocky slopes from 300 to 1,000 metres elevation. It is threatened by overharvesting."
    }
